{
  "summary": "The previous proposal correctly identifies the root cause (on_restart callback not wired up in tui.py's ServerClient instantiation) and the JS confirm/alert issue, but it has several gaps: (1) It overlooks that action_restart() is synchronous while ServerClient expects on_restart to be async (Callable[[], Awaitable[None]]) — a naive wiring would fail or block the event loop, so an async wrapper method (e.g., _handle_restart) is needed that dispatches to the sync action_restart via call_from_thread or similar. (2) action_restart() requires self.selected_feature to be set or it silently returns with a warning — a remote restart from the webui has no concept of a 'selected feature', so the proposal needs to clarify what the restart actually restarts when triggered remotely (the entire TUI process? the pipeline for a specific item? all running agents?). Without resolving this ambiguity, the fix could wire up the callback but still effectively do nothing. (3) The proposal mentions client.html and index.html both need modal conversion but doesn't note that index.html already uses showToast() for success while client.html uses alert() — the two files have diverged, and the modal implementation needs to account for both templates having different existing modal infrastructure. (4) There's no consideration of race conditions: if the user triggers restart from the webui while the TUI is mid-pipeline-run, action_restart's _run_restart_async spawns a new AgentRunner without canceling the existing one, potentially causing conflicting concurrent pipeline operations."
}
